00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.510 align:start position:0%
 
remember it was under donald trump we  had 1.4 inflation we were energy  independent we were a net exporter of  energy our border was secure and safety  and security we had at home and abroad  as we were was respected as a country  and donald trump accomplished all of  that while simultaneously dealing with  conspiracy theories one hoax after  another one lie after another one phony  investigation after another now all of  it undone by joe biden in 18 short  months now president trump's successors  are chronicled in a new book by former  senior advisor and son-in-law jared  kushner he joins us now he's the author  of the book it's in bookstores all  around the country and of course  amazon.com breaking history a white  house memoir  you know the amazing thing um you're a  part of history most people will never  really truly understand  what life is really like in that house  and what goes on behind the scenes  there's no doubt about it that  any objective  observation of the trump presidency it  was a consequential presidency  and we see after 18 months what can  happen  when you abandon the policies that your  father-in-law instituted in this country  what was it about him what did you see  about him that made him that different  so first of all sean it's great to be  with you it was a great honor to serve  and president trump took the  responsibility  very seriously to fight for the american  people and keep his promises you were  speaking earlier about all the different  accomplishments he was able to have  economically those weren't an accident  it's been awful to watch the inflation  that's happened the rise in gas prices  but all that happened under the guise of  all the investigations and attacks and i  read extensively in the book it really  is everyone who's read it have said that  it's a very fast-paced read and that's  because i weave together all the efforts  to try to push forward on the different  policies while simultaneously dealing  with all these false investigations that  we had to fend off because even though  they were based on uh crazy accusations  from the beginning whether it was the  russia hoax or trying to you know get  trump or impeach him for trying to  investigate corruption in ukraine they  were serious accusations and we had to  take it and you know one story i tell in  the book too is how president trump  negotiated a deal between saudi arabia  and russia in order to save our oil and  gas industry which now the current  administration has hampered which could  be bringing down the price of gas in  this country very quickly if allowed to  and it was a really intense negotiation  but president trump got along with  people in the world he got along with  vladimir putin he got along with  president xi it didn't mean he didn't  have tough discussions with them but i  really go through the way that he dealt  with them which is how he kept the world  peaceful all the critics who again you  know that were lying about the trump  administration for four years they were  saying that if trump was elected he  would lead to world war three but we had  six peace deals during trump's time and  the world was a very very safe place so  i would go through all that extensively  in the book let me ask you this then  because he did it while being  investigated what three years on  trump-russia collusion that never  happened he did it during an impeachment  all this happened and then covet hit and  and that threw the world upside down how  did he do it  while simultaneously having to deal with  all that stress that probably would have  crushed a million other people  well if you would ask him that he would  say do i have a choice you know he was  elected he had a big responsibility and  uh and it was very very hard and we were  very grateful again i would you know be  at night i'd turn on your show and i  would you know see yourself greg jarrod  solomon uh you know sarah carter uh  going off and basically saying all this  stuff is debunked and then i flip over  to msnbc and i would see them saying  they're right on the heels they're about  to get these guys and i'm saying but we  didn't do anything and you know you  really had to just block that off and  just focus on the different things that  we wanted to do and president trump was  very focused one of the efforts that i  worked on that i detailed in the book  was the efforts in the middle east to  try to bring peace between israel and  the arab countries and that's something  that the conventional thinking was that  it would never happen but president  trump was an outsider he brought a  businessman's approach to washington  businessmen are results driven unlike  politicians who generally wanted just to  process  there are some great politicians too but  i write about how an outsider with  without a lot of political experience uh  and a team came in and were able to  achieve results that the political uh  career people were not able to achieve  and so the book really goes through the  detail  all right two-part question  one is speculation on your part maybe  you do know something that we don't know  do you think he's going to run  and when you factor in all the your  family went through and we're talking  about don jr and eric and laura and  ivanka and the whole family when you  factor all of that in do you want him to  would you want to go through that again  well it still continues for a lot of the  family  so first of all i i don't want to speak  for him and obviously he is very  bothered by what he's seeing happen in  the country he did a great job keeping  our economy strong keeping our world  safe  and really fighting for american  industry and i think that he knows that  he could fix it very quickly but it is a  big toll again he's constantly under  siege it was a big toll on on the entire  family but i think that the way we all  viewed it is that the cost of of service  and all the attacks and uh what was was  was very small relative to the impact  that  president trump and his administration  were able to make for on so many people  and their families you know one thing we  worked on that you were very supportive  was our criminal justice reform where we  were helping people who made mistakes in  their lives re-enter society with  training and job skills so that they  don't commit crimes in the future all  those people are given a new lease on  life all the pardons the alice marie  johnson's that president trump were able  to give help give second chances to that  was incredible work which you know when  you think about that it really you know  puts all the pain and stuff in context  and so for me writing the book it i  always like to look forwards not  backwards but it really was a reminder  of that brutal first year when we had a  lot of different people trying to find  their way in the white house again we  were being accused of colluding with  russia which was a crazy notion i mean i  would look at it and say you know most  days i couldn't collude on the campaign  with donald and we could include with  our field office in iowa yet they were  saying we pulled off this whole  elaborate scheme  but the same people who are pushing that  false narrative are the same people who  are continuously attacking president  trump and a lot of the republican party  who are fighting just to you know fight  for the middle class and in order to  give them jobs and give them opportunity  and to keep our country safe  it's called breaking history bookstores  everywhere amazon.com if you want to  sign copy jaredkushnerbooks.com  uh jared appreciate you being with us  and uh i learned a lot and i thought i  knew a lot about what was going on and  there was a lot i didn't know that was  going on thanks for being with us hey  sean hannity here hey click here to  subscribe to fox news youtube page and  catch our hottest interviews and most  compelling analysis you will not get it  anywhere else

